\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces Historical parameter sensitivity for three 4k rankings, with $k=5$, $W=320$ and step coupling. Each panel is one contact graph; each point is the mean paired spread difference over ten paths, and bars are one path standard deviation. Settings are discrete, not a continuous sweep. Vertical scales differ between panels. Positive differences favor the restricted set. The default $(.01,3)$ reuses the budget scan. These are path-variation bars, not conditional Monte Carlo intervals or uncertainty across networks.}}{18}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hist-parameters}{{S5}{18}{Historical parameter sensitivity for three 4k rankings, with $k=5$, $W=320$ and step coupling. Each panel is one contact graph; each point is the mean paired spread difference over ten paths, and bars are one path standard deviation. Settings are discrete, not a continuous sweep. Vertical scales differ between panels. Positive differences favor the restricted set. The default $(.01,3)$ reuses the budget scan. These are path-variation bars, not conditional Monte Carlo intervals or uncertainty across networks}{figure.5}{}}
